  "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story. Asset type: Japanese elementary vocabulary illustrations, sheet 57. Edit the provided 2048x2048 template, painting ONLY inside its sixteen white panels. Every single panel MUST have identical width and height. All horizontal lines must be EXACTLY at 0%,25%,50%,75%,100%, not based on artwork. Keep precisely the 4x4 equal grid and 5 continuous pure magenta #ff00ff lines in each direction, including outer frame. Preserve line position, width and full canvas. Each panel is an independent clear gentle picture-book illustration as isolated vignettes on a pure white background, large and easily understood. Never use magenta for illustration. Avoid all pink, purple and neon colors in artwork, objects, decorations, lighting and shadows. Use warm orange, red, yellow, green, blue and neutral colors. No pink/purple concert lights. Nothing crosses the grid. No text, letters, numbers, labels, symbols resembling writing or watermarks. For abstract words show a concrete situation illustrating the meaning. Diverse natural children and adults, no stereotypes. Correct anatomy and objects. Panels in strict row-major order (left to right, top to bottom):\n1. 初歩 — 学び始めるときの基礎の部分。\n2. 署名 — 自分の名前を書くことや書かれた名前。\n3. 書物 — 本のこと。\n4. 所有 — 自分の物として持っていること。\n5. 書類 — 用事や記録などをまとめて書いた文書。\n6. ショー — 歌や演技などを人に見せる催し。\n7. ショール — 肩などに掛ける大きな布。\n8. 白髪 — 白くなった髪の毛。\n9. 知らせ — 人に伝える事柄や連絡。\n10. 知り合い — 互いに知っている人。\n11. 視力 — 目でものの形などを見分ける力。\n12. シリーズ — 共通した内容で続いている作品などのまとまり。\n13. シルク — 蚕の繭から作る絹。\n14. 印 — 何かを見分けたり示したりする目当て。\n15. シルバー — 銀や銀色。\n16. 白地 — 白い色の下地。\nSafety and clarity: Vehicles must be driven only by unmistakable adults, never children. Industrial machinery and knives are used by adults. Do not put a child in a car driver's seat. Keep artwork separated by the measured template grid.\nDo not add numerical claims, prices, quantities, currency denominations, calorie values or stroke-order numbers unless explicitly required by the target word. Mathematical concepts should have neutral concrete examples without unverified numeric diagrams.\n",
